      <main>
        <!-- HERO -->
        <section class="hero">
          <div class="col">
            <div class="brandblock" data-reveal>
              <p class="brandname">PROOFWORKS</p>
              <p class="brandsub">Founder thesis by Kyle Findlay</p>
            </div>
            <h1 class="hero-head" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.06s">Job titles are <span class="accent">lagging indicators.</span></h1>
            <p class="hero-lead" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.14s">Proofworks retools the operators companies already have — dispatchers, coordinators, account managers, estimators — into people who can rebuild their own workflows with AI. <b>Companies pay for the result.</b></p>
            <div class="cta-row" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.2s">
              <a href="mailto:kylefindlay828@gmail.com?subject=Let's%20talk%20about%20Proofworks" class="btn-g">Start a conversation →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- LINEAGE (compact, low-key) -->
        <section class="sec" style="padding:36px 0 0">
          <div class="col">
            <p class="lin-mini" data-reveal>
              <span class="lead">My third build.</span>
              <a href="/gtm-radar">GTM Radar V1</a><span class="s">→</span><a href="/radar-v2">GTM Radar V2</a><span class="s">→</span><span class="now">Proofworks</span>
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- THE WEDGE -->
        <section class="sec">
          <div class="col">
            <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>The wedge</p>
            <h2 class="w-h" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.05s">Retool the operators a company already trusts.</h2>

            <div class="w-block" data-reveal>
              <p class="w-k">Who pays</p>
              <p class="w-b big">Mid-market companies outside tech. Home services, logistics, healthcare admin, field and frontline commercial. A national plumbing company runs on dispatchers, estimators, and account reps. A logistics firm runs on coordinators. A hospital network runs on schedulers and claims teams. Every one of them employs operators whose real ability their title never describes.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="w-block" data-reveal>
              <p class="w-k">What they buy</p>
              <p class="w-b" style="margin-bottom:14px"><b>It starts with one workflow.</b></p>
              <p class="w-steps">A few operators, one real workflow each, rebuilt with AI and measured against how it ran before. That is the entry. Their work keeps changing, so the retooling continues: new workflows, new operators, systems that stay current. The company keeps the systems and the operators. Proofworks stays in the work.</p>
              <p class="w-b" style="margin-top:16px">Priced as an ongoing engagement, scoped to each company. It starts small and grows as the retooling reaches more workflows and more operators.</p>
              <p class="w-keeper"><b>No courses, no certificates.</b> Operators rebuild the real workflows they run every day, and the working result is the proof.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="w-block" data-reveal>
              <p class="w-k">Why the employer pays</p>
              <p class="w-b">They are buying a measured outcome on people they already trust. Not a course, not a new hire. These operators know the business. Proofworks makes them faster and leaves systems behind.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- PROOF -->
        <section class="sec">
          <div class="col">
            <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Proof</p>
            <p class="proof-lead" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.05s">Proof over claims. Pilot results will live here as they come in.</p>
            <p class="proof-b" data-reveal>For now, the work is the proof. <b>GTM Radar V2 is live:</b> an autonomous agent that catches hiring signals before the role is posted. Same instinct, already shipped.</p>
            <div class="cta-row" data-reveal>
              <a href="/radar-v2" class="btn-g">See GTM Radar V2 →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- WHY THIS FOUNDER -->
        <section class="sec">
          <div class="col">
            <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Why this founder</p>
            <p class="why-stmt" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.05s">For years I ran operations built on exactly these people. I saw what they could do the moment someone handed them better tools.</p>
            <p class="mission" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.1s">Proofworks is how I help people help themselves. Give an operator the ability to rebuild their own work and they carry it for the rest of their career. <b>That is the problem I am solving, and it is the mission.</b></p>
            <div class="stat-grid" style="margin-top:36px">
              <div class="stat" data-reveal>
                <div class="statnum" style="color:var(--g)" data-count data-count-to="3.1" data-count-dec="1" data-count-prefix="$" data-count-suffix="M+">$3.1M+</div>
                <div class="statlbl">owned annually</div>
              </div>
              <div class="stat" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.08s">
                <div class="statnum" style="color:var(--c)">$5–6M</div>
                <div class="statlbl">supported</div>
              </div>
              <div class="stat" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.16s">
                <div class="statnum" style="color:var(--v)">30–40</div>
                <div class="statlbl">programs / year</div>
              </div>
              <div class="stat" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.24s">
                <div class="statnum" style="color:var(--g)" data-count data-count-to="12" data-count-dec="0" data-count-suffix="+">12+</div>
                <div class="statlbl">national brands</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="why-close" data-reveal style="margin-top:32px"><b style="color:#eef1f4">Solo founder, moving fast,</b> relocating to San Francisco. Open to technical cofounders working at the intersection of AI, talent, and operator workflows.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- WHAT IT BECOMES -->
        <section class="sec">
          <div class="col">
            <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>What it becomes</p>
            <p class="becomes" data-reveal style="transition-delay:.05s">Every paid engagement produces operators whose ability is proven on real work. Across enough companies, those operators become <b>a network no job board can match,</b> with demand pulling supply in. <span class="dim">The employer wedge comes first; the network is what it unlocks later.</span></p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- CONTACT -->
        <section class="sec" id="contact">
          <div class="col">
            <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Get in touch</p>
            <div class="contact-panel" data-reveal>
              <div class="contact-row">
                <div class="who">
                  <div class="avatar"><Image src={headshot} alt="Kyle Findlay" width={360} height={450} /></div>
                  <div>
                    <div class="nm">Kyle Findlay</div>
                    <div class="loc">San Francisco / Los Angeles</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="contact-actions">
                  <button id="copy-email" class="btn-g" data-email={email} type="button"><span class="ce">Copy email</span> ⧉</button>
                  <a href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pill-out">LinkedIn ↗</a>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p class="contact-email">{email}</p>
              <p style="font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(18px,2.1vw,24px);line-height:1.25;color:#eef1f4;margin:20px 0 0">Talking to <span style="color:var(--g)">companies about pilots, and to technical cofounders about building this.</span></p>
            </div>
            <div class="foot">
              <a href="/">About &amp; Contact</a>
              <a href="/gtm-radar">GTM Radar V1</a>
              <a href="/radar-v2">GTM Radar V2</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>

    <script>
      // ── animated background: aurora blobs (hue-drift) + constellation network ──
      (() => {
        const canvas = document.getElementById('bg');
        if (!(canvas instanceof HTMLCanvasElement)) return;
        const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
        if (!ctx) return;
        const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
        let W = 0, H = 0;
        function resize() {
          const dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
          W = window.innerWidth; H = window.innerHeight;
          canvas.width = W * dpr; canvas.height = H * dpr;
          ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
        }
        resize();
        window.addEventListener('resize', resize);
        // cursor state — dots part around it and link to it
        const mouse = { x: null, y: null };
        if (!reduce) {
          window.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => { mouse.x = e.clientX / W; mouse.y = e.clientY / H; }, { passive: true });
          window.addEventListener('mouseout', (e) => { if (!e.relatedTarget) { mouse.x = mouse.y = null; } });
          window.addEventListener('blur', () => { mouse.x = mouse.y = null; });
        }
        const blobs = [
          { hue: 138, r: .44, ox: .26, oy: .34, ax: .12, ay: .10, sx: .075, sy: .055, hs: 5, op: 0.6, sr: .090, so: .070 },   // green (reduced, stays on-page)
          { hue: 224, r: .56, ox: .74, oy: .40, ax: .13, ay: .12, sx: .105, sy: .125, hs: -6, op: 1.5, sr: .110, so: .085 }, // blue (clear blue)
          { hue: 282, r: .52, ox: .50, oy: .70, ax: .14, ay: .11, sx: .130, sy: .085, hs: 8, op: 1.25, sr: .080, so: .100 },  // purple
        ];
        const N = 230, pts = [];
        for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) pts.push({ x: Math.random(), y: Math.random(), vx: (Math.random() - .5) * 0.00012, vy: (Math.random() - .5) * 0.00012 });
        const start = performance.now();
        const maxD = 0.062;
        function frame(now) {
          const t = (now - start) / 1000;
          ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
          ctx.fillStyle = '#06070a'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
          ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter';
          for (const b of blobs) {
            const cx = (b.ox + Math.sin(t * b.sx) * b.ax) * W;
            const cy = (b.oy + Math.cos(t * b.sy) * b.ay) * H;
            const rad = b.r * Math.max(W, H) * 0.5 * (1 + Math.sin(t * (b.sr ?? .08) + b.hue) * 0.15);
            const hue = b.hue + Math.sin(t * 0.12) * b.hs;
            const op = (b.op ?? 1) * (0.88 + 0.14 * Math.sin(t * (b.so ?? .08) + b.r * 12));
            const g = ctx.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, 0, cx, cy, rad);
            g.addColorStop(0, `hsla(${hue}, 90%, 72%, ${0.42 * op})`);
            g.addColorStop(0.3, `hsla(${hue}, 85%, 60%, ${0.22 * op})`);
            g.addColorStop(0.66, `hsla(${hue}, 75%, 48%, ${0.07 * op})`);
            g.addColorStop(1, `hsla(${hue}, 70%, 45%, 0)`);
            ctx.fillStyle = g;
            ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(cx, cy, rad, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
          }
          ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
          const hasM = mouse.x !== null;
          const mpx = hasM ? mouse.x * W : 0, mpy = hasM ? mouse.y * H : 0;
          const Rpx = 0.13 * Math.min(W, H);   // repel radius around cursor
          const linkR = 0.12 * Math.min(W, H); // cursor-to-dot link radius
          // advance dots + compute rendered positions (parting around the cursor)
          for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
            const p = pts[i];
            if (!reduce) {
              p.x += p.vx; p.y += p.vy;
              if (p.x < 0 || p.x > 1) p.vx *= -1;
              if (p.y < 0 || p.y > 1) p.vy *= -1;
              p.x = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, p.x)); p.y = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, p.y));
            }
            let rx = p.x * W, ry = p.y * H;
            if (hasM) {
              const ex = rx - mpx, ey = ry - mpy, ed = Math.hypot(ex, ey);
              if (ed < Rpx && ed > 0.001) {
                const push = ((Rpx - ed) / Rpx) ** 2 * 46;
                rx += (ex / ed) * push; ry += (ey / ed) * push;
              }
            }
            p.rx = rx; p.ry = ry;
          }
          // links between nearby dots
          for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
            const p = pts[i];
            for (let j = i + 1; j < N; j++) {
              const q = pts[j];
              const dx = p.x - q.x, dy = p.y - q.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy);
              if (d < maxD) {
                ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(180,200,210,${0.10 * (1 - d / maxD)})`;
                ctx.lineWidth = 1;
                ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(p.rx, p.ry); ctx.lineTo(q.rx, q.ry); ctx.stroke();
              }
            }
          }
          // links from the cursor to nearby dots
          if (hasM) {
            for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
              const p = pts[i];
              const dx = p.rx - mpx, dy = p.ry - mpy, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy);
              if (d < linkR) {
                ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(150,225,190,${0.5 * (1 - d / linkR)})`;
                ctx.lineWidth = 1;
                ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(mpx, mpy); ctx.lineTo(p.rx, p.ry); ctx.stroke();
              }
            }
          }
          for (const p of pts) {
            ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(200,215,225,0.5)';
            ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.rx, p.ry, 1.3, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
          }
          if (!reduce) requestAnimationFrame(frame);
        }
        requestAnimationFrame(frame);
      })();

      // ── scroll reveal + count-up ──
      (() => {
        const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
        function countUp(el) {
          const to = parseFloat(el.dataset.countTo || '0');
          const dec = parseInt(el.dataset.countDec || '0', 10);
          const pre = el.dataset.countPrefix || '', suf = el.dataset.countSuffix || '';
          const dur = 1200, start = performance.now();
          const token = (el._ct = (el._ct || 0) + 1); // supersede any in-flight run
          function step(now) {
            if (el._ct !== token) return;
            const p = Math.min(1, (now - start) / dur);
            const e = 1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 3);
            el.textContent = pre + (to * e).toFixed(dec) + suf;
            if (p < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);
          }
          requestAnimationFrame(step);
        }
        const els = document.querySelectorAll('[data-reveal]');
        if (reduce || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
          els.forEach((el) => el.classList.add('in'));
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-count]').forEach((el) => countUp(el));
          return;
        }
        // reveal on first enter; never un-reveal on leave (so mid-page scrolling
        // up/down never re-triggers).
        const obs = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          entries.forEach((e) => {
            if (e.isIntersecting && !e.target.classList.contains('in')) {
              e.target.classList.add('in');
              const c = e.target.querySelector('[data-count]');
              if (c) countUp(c);
            }
          });
        }, { threshold: 0.12, rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px' });
        els.forEach((el) => obs.observe(el));

        // only when the user returns to the very top do we clear the reveals that
        // are below the fold — so the next scroll down replays every animation.
        let armed = false;
        window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
          if (window.scrollY > 400) armed = true;
          else if (window.scrollY <= 2 && armed) {
            armed = false;
            const vh = window.innerHeight;
            els.forEach((el) => {
              if (el.getBoundingClientRect().top >= vh) el.classList.remove('in');
            });
          }
        }, { passive: true });
      })();

      // ── copy email (every button with data-email — hero + contact) ──
      document.querySelectorAll('button[data-email]').forEach((btn) => {
        const label = btn.querySelector('.ce');
        const original = label ? label.textContent : '';
        btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
          try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.email || ''); }
          catch { const t = document.createElement('textarea'); t.value = btn.dataset.email || ''; document.body.appendChild(t); t.select(); document.execCommand('copy'); t.remove(); }
          if (label) { label.textContent = 'Copied!'; setTimeout(() => { label.textContent = original; }, 1600); }
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
